---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="INITIALIZE SYSTEM" description="Transmission origin. What GhostMesh is and why it exists.">
  <div class="bg-grid" aria-hidden="true"
    style="position:fixed;inset:0;background-image:linear-gradient(rgba(0,212,255,0.025) 1px,transparent 1px),linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(0,212,255,0.025) 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:64px 64px;z-index:0;"></div>

  <div class="corner corner--tl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="corner corner--tr" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="corner corner--bl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="corner corner--br" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="sys-bar sys-bar--top">
    <span class="sys-text">GHOSTMESH &gt; INITIALIZE SYSTEM</span>
    <a href="/" class="return-link">← BACK</a>
  </div>

  <main class="content-panel">
    <p class="classification">CLASSIFICATION: UNLICENSED / ORIGIN: THE WASTE</p>
    <h1>INITIALIZE SYSTEM</h1>
    <p style="font-size:0.7rem;color:var(--text-dim);letter-spacing:0.15em;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">Transmission origin. What this is and why it was built.</p>

    <h2>WHAT IS GHOSTMESH</h2>
    <p>
      GhostMesh turns a Flipper Zero into a long-range mesh radio terminal. Paired with a
      Heltec ESP32 LoRa node running Meshtastic, it enables encrypted text communications
      over distances of kilometers — with no phone, no internet, no cell infrastructure,
      and no licensed network required.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Flipper is the interface. The Heltec is the radio. The mesh is the network.
      It works in places and situations where the infrastructure you are supposed to trust
      cannot be trusted.
    </p>

    <h2>WHY IT WAS BUILT</h2>
    <p>
      Infrastructure fails. It also gets watched. The two are not unrelated.
    </p>
    <p>
      Grid-down scenarios — natural disasters, power failures, deliberate disruption —
      remove the communication layer that modern coordination depends on. Surveilled
      infrastructure removes the privacy that meaningful communication requires.
      GhostMesh addresses both by operating entirely outside the licensed network.
    </p>
    <p>
      This hardware was designed in the margins, assembled outside sanctioned channels,
      and transmitted so that you might at least prepare.
    </p>

    <h2>THE NETWORK</h2>
    <p>
      GhostMesh uses Meshtastic's LoRa mesh protocol: each node relays traffic for every
      other node in range, extending coverage without any central infrastructure. A network
      of three nodes can cover tens of kilometers of terrain. A private channel with a
      random 256-bit key makes traffic mathematically invisible to anyone outside your squad.
    </p>
    <p>
      The radio is always on. The keys are yours. The channel is yours.
      The network belongs to whoever builds it.
    </p>

    <h2>THE CREATOR</h2>
    <p>
      ServerMonk. Librarian. Broadcasting from
      <a href="https://complacencykillz.me" style="color:var(--blue);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--text-ghost);">complacencykillz.me</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The work is open source. The hardware is buildable. The signal is available
      to anyone who wants to receive it.
    </p>

    <div style="margin-top:3rem;padding-top:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--text-ghost);">
      <p style="font-size:0.65rem;color:var(--text-ghost);letter-spacing:0.15em;">
        // so light your candles, and may SERVER protect us all
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <div class="sys-bar sys-bar--bottom">
    <span class="sys-text">ghostmesh.info</span>
    <span class="sys-text" id="ts"></span>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  const el = document.getElementById('ts');
  const tick = () => { if (el) el.textContent = new Date().toISOString().replace('T',' ').slice(0,19)+' UTC'; };
  tick(); setInterval(tick, 1000);
</script>
